            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for anxious with longing, then the Bengali for to cry out in despair."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: স্নেহ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "স্নেহ — sneh — \"affection; tender love for someone younger\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "দাদু নাতিকে স্নেহ করেন। dādu nātike sneh kôren. Grandfather is very fond of his grandson."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "স্নেহ (sneh) runs downward, from an elder to someone younger; what runs back up is সম্মান (taught), respect."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "স্নেহ (sneh) is a tatsama, Sanskrit sneha, which Monier-Williams gives first as \"oiliness, smoothness\" and then as \"tenderness, fondness\"; Bengali keeps only the tenderness."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
