          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "মায়া — māyā — \"tender attachment; fond pity\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "পুরনো বাড়িটা ছাড়তে আমার মায়া লাগল। purôno bāṛiṭā chhāṛte āmār māyā lāglô. Leaving the old house, I felt a pang of attachment."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "মায়া (māyā) is the soft pull you feel toward a person, a pet or a place; the older sense, illusion, belongs to philosophy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "মায়া (māyā) is a tatsama, Sanskrit māyā, \"supernatural power, illusion\" (CDIAL 10060), where CDIAL, like Monier-Williams, also records a sense of compassion, from the lexicographers; the everyday Bengali sense of tender attachment probably grew from that one."
            }
          ]
        },
