          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ভক্তি করা — bhôkti kôrā — \"to be devoted to; to revere (an elder)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "আমার ভাই বাবাকে খুব ভক্তি করে। āmār bhāi bābāke khub bhôkti kôre. My brother is deeply devoted to our father."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): তিনি তাঁর বাবাকে ভক্তি করতেন, tini tā̃r bābāke bhôkti kôrten."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "স্নেহ (sneh) goes down, to someone younger; ভক্তি goes up, to a parent, an elder or a god."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ভক্তি করা (bhôkti kôrā) puts ভক্তি, the tatsama Sanskrit bhakti, devotion and fond attachment (Monier-Williams), before করা, to do. ভক্ত, a devotee, is the related Sanskrit bhakta."
            }
          ]
        },
